# PyCharm
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
.idea/

# --- Course-repo additions -------------------------------------------------
# Microsoft Office lock/owner files. This repo is full of .docx/.pptx, and Word
# and PowerPoint drop a "~$name.docx" stub next to any file that is open.
~$*

# LibreOffice lock/owner files. soffice drops a ".~lock.name.pdf#" beside any
# file it has open, and the slide leg of the build runs soffice over this repo,
# so these turn up in student-facing module folders.
.~lock.*#

# Windows equivalents of .DS_Store (macOS's is covered above)
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Quarto build output
_site/
.quarto/

# --- Never publish -----------------------------------------------------------
# build_reading.py writes a dot-prefixed temp HTML next to the reading and
# removes it when the run succeeds. A CRASHED run leaves it behind, and since
# --push runs `git add -A`, an orphan would be committed to the live site. This
# has already happened twice.
.*_reading_*.html

# Scratch that lives inside the site repo but must never reach the website.
_to_delete/
